<worksheet>
    <title>LT 1-2 Tortoise and Hare
    <subtitle>Adapted from Amplify Classroom and "Beginning Algebra Made Useful"</subtitle>
</title>
<exercise>
    <statement>
        <p>
            The tortoise and the hare are racing. The tortoise starts at the starting line and runs at a constant speed.  The hare also starts at the starting line but runs at a faster pace for several minutes.  He then realizes that the tortoise is slow, so he stops to take a nap.  When he wakes up, he sees that the tortoise has passed him, so he starts running again.  He catches up to the tortoise at the finish line.
        </p>
        <p>
            Use the information provided to answer the following questions:
        </p>
    </statement>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p> Which animal does each function represent in the graph?  Label the graph with "Tortoise" and "Hare".  
            </p>
            <p> Explain your thinking.</p>
        
            <figure xml:id="fig-tortoise-hare">
                <image source="tandhare.png" width="40%"/>
                <shortdescription>A ditance and time graph graph with a constant increasing graph starting at (9,0), and a linear graph that increases, then is contant, and ends incrasing.</shortdescription>
            </figure>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>    
        <statement>
            <p>
                This graph shows the relatioship between the distance and time for a third animal, the fox.
            </p>
        
         <figure xml:id="fig-fox-graph">
            <image source="tandhareandfox.png" width="40%"/>
            <shortdescription>A distance and time graph with a constant graph starting at (9,0), a linear graph that increases, then is constant, and ends increasing, and a third graph that starts at (6,0) and is constant</shortdescription>  
        </figure>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.1in">
        <statement>
            <p>
               Tell a story about the fox's journey during the race.  Include specific details about time and distance.
            </p>
           
        </statement>
    </task>
</exercise>
</worksheet>
